  "security_implications": "status_alert_fatal_fault latches any assertion of alert_fatal (even transient) and stays high until system reset. This sticky behavior prevents a fatal security fault (e.g., cryptographic integrity failure, tamper detect) from being missed, ensuring the system can halt or wipe secrets as needed. Absence of a software-clearable path prevents an attacker from masking such faults.",
